# Installation CLIs.
#
# Executables your own jobs, harvesters and sensors depend on. Kernel code
# that can use an optional provider finds it with optionalBin() in
# lib/ext-hooks.mjs: $<ENV_VAR>, else bin/_ext/<name>, else bin/<name>, else
# none (the feature is skipped). Names the kernel asks for:
#
#   apple-weather   JSON weather for the weather sensor (EDVA_WEATHER_BIN)
#   location-ask closers used by bin/hum-ping (see that file)
#
# bin/edva-send-curl's event geo-gate takes two optional CLIs: an itinerary
# check, `<cli> in-city <city> <date>` (EDVA_TRAVEL_BIN), and a
# must-see-performer check that bypasses the gate, `<cli> check <name>`
# (EDVA_HEADLINER_BIN); point those variables at copies kept here.
# bin/hum-sense kicks bin/watch when it exists (with lib/_ext/watches.mjs).
#
# Everything here except this file is gitignored — see .gitignore and
# docs/architecture-public-private.md.
